/**
 * The game's clip lengths, motion-type bits, run numbers and command classes behind the per-command action time (re-parity lane X2-A,
 * row XA6 slice A; **FFX-2 only**). Numbers only, in our ids: motion-set numbers, frame counts, command-row ids. No game text, no file names.
 * Generated by a script from the game's own frame tables (the lane's `gen_action_frames.py`); every number below is read, none is tuned.
 *
 * Sources. Note FFX2-G01 sections 7, 8 and 16 (the frame tables of 54 girl and 306 monster motion sets, the motion-type bits and the run
 * numbers of the monsters' and girls' motion macros) and note FFX2-G11 sections 2, 3 and 6 (the stages of a command, the measured lengths).
 * The scene geometry is FFX2-G07's table (35 scenes, 102 girl-to-nearest-monster pairs). Command classes and effect ids are the rows' own
 * bytes (`kernel/command.bin`, `kernel/monmagic.bin` via `ffx2-abil.mjs`) for the 488 rows our data names.
 *
 * What is measured, what is read and what is an estimate (every estimate is labelled; none is a game number):
 * - READ [D]: the clip lengths below, the motion-type bits, the run speed and attack-start distance of each body, each row's class and effect id.
 * - MEASURED [M] (2026-10-09 live session, `research/re-ffx2-timing-measured.md`): the release-to-completion length of three effects:
 *   Fire (effect 76) 75 steps on a girl; a monster cast of effect 176 (Umbral Gaze, `Lingering Gaze` shares the effect) 94, 94 and 94 steps (a fourth
 *   was 114 while it waited behind another effect); a monster cast of effect 368 (Strength Up) 84 steps. These totals include whatever start-gate wait the
 *   measured body had, so no separate gate term is added (the monsters' chant loop clip is absent from 28 of the 36 sets below, so the clip playing at
 *   release cannot be named from the tables).
 * - ESTIMATE [I]: every other effect length takes the class default below (75 for a girl's, 94 for an enemy's); the run-up uses the median
 *   starting distance and the macro's run speed as units a second with no ramp or turning (a lower bound); the idle wait is half the idle clip.
 */

/** Motion-type bits (the game's header names), as the macros set them. */
export const MT_RUN_00_01 = 0x1;
export const MT_RUN_01 = 0x2;
export const MT_CHANT_START_WAIT = 0x80;
export const MT_MAGIC_THROW_WAIT = 0x100;
export const MT_IDLE_WAIT = 0x200;
export const MT_ENERGY_ATTACK = 0x4000;

/** A girl's motion set: `[idle1, attack1_00, magic2_00, skill_00, item_00]` in motion frames (0 = no such clip). */
export type GirlFrames = readonly [idle: number, attack: number, castStart: number, skillStart: number, itemStart: number];

/** A monster's motion set: `[idle1 (idle2 if none), attack1_00, magic2_00, skill_00, motion-type bits, run speed, attack-start distance]`. */
export type MonsterFrames = readonly [idle: number, attack: number, castStart: number, skillStart: number, bits: number, runSpeed: number, startDist: number];

